  <p>If you're the adult child reading this for a parent, worried and not sure how to raise it, you're doing a loving thing. Bringing it up gently is often the hardest part. You're welcome to make the free call yourself to talk through how to approach it, before anyone commits to anything.</p>
  <p>And if you're the older adult here on your own steam, wondering whether therapy is really for people like you: it is. You've earned a place to be honest about the hard parts of a long life. That's not weakness. That's wisdom about what actually helps.</p>
